       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours means toxicity would last a long time. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't justify a dose this high.\n\nIt may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or a lower starting dose\n\nIf you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was intentionally confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
